== (3) two-variable law M_extra = K (sigma/200 km/s)^a (r/100 kpc)^b  [form B]
   best: log K = 10.82, a = 4.17 (68% 4.07-4.30; 95% 4.00-4.41), b = 0.41 (68% 0.38-0.45; 95% 0.34-0.47); rms 0.126
   correlation of a and b across bootstrap: -0.84
   a=3,b=3 (max phase-space density, packed) : log K = 9.14, rms 0.170 (vs free 0.126); n*Delta(MSE) class-balanced = 0.0132 dex^2
   a=2,b=1 (isothermal halo)                 : log K = 11.18, rms 0.161 (vs free 0.126); n*Delta(MSE) class-balanced = 0.0101 dex^2
   M_extra = c M_b                           : c = 0.302, rms 0.174
   RAR only                                  : rms 0.189
   a=b=3 normalisation -> fermion mass (Pauli bound F = g m^4/h^3, Maxwellian core, g=2): 1.26 eV  (Tremaine-Gunn F<=g m^4/(2h^3) gives x2^(1/4)=1.50 eV)
   a=b=3 normalisation -> fermion mass (Pauli bound F = g m^4/h^3, Maxwellian core, g=1): 1.50 eV  (Tremaine-Gunn F<=g m^4/(2h^3) gives x2^(1/4)=1.79 eV)

